#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:1
msgid "This is a sample YODL document used to test the po4a YODL parser."
msgstr "THIS IS A SAMPLE YODL DOCUMENT USED TO TEST THE PO4A YODL PARSER."

#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:3
msgid ""
"The tt(yodl) program reads one or more input files and writes one output "
"file.  Inline macros such as em(italic) stay inside the whole paragraph, and "
"so does a link(fall back to)(plainhtml) command with several arguments."
msgstr ""
"THE TT(YODL) PROGRAM READS ONE OR MORE INPUT FILES AND WRITES ONE OUTPUT "
"FILE.  INLINE MACROS SUCH AS EM(ITALIC) STAY INSIDE THE WHOLE PARAGRAPH, AND "
"SO DOES A LINK(FALL BACK TO)(PLAINHTML) COMMAND WITH SEVERAL ARGUMENTS."

#. type: center
#: basic.yo:8
msgid "tt(yodl) em(flags) em(inputfile) em([inputfile...])"
msgstr "TT(YODL) EM(FLAGS) EM(INPUTFILE) EM([INPUTFILE...])"

#. type: itemization/it
#: basic.yo:12
msgid "tt(-D) em(name): Defines em(name) as a symbol."
msgstr "TT(-D) EM(NAME): DEFINES EM(NAME) AS A SYMBOL."

#. type: itemization/it
#: basic.yo:13
msgid "tt(-I) em(directory): Searches include files in a directory."
msgstr "TT(-I) EM(DIRECTORY): SEARCHES INCLUDE FILES IN A DIRECTORY."

#. type: description/dit
#: basic.yo:17
msgid "tt(-N) em(number)"
msgstr "TT(-N) EM(NUMBER)"

#. type: description/dit
#: basic.yo:18
msgid "Sets the counter em(number) to the given value."
msgstr "SETS THE COUNTER EM(NUMBER) TO THE GIVEN VALUE."

#. type: chapter
#: basic.yo:21
msgid "Using the yodl program"
msgstr "USING THE YODL PROGRAM"

#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:23
msgid "Some text containing the"
msgstr "SOME TEXT CONTAINING THE"

#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:23
msgid "macro, which is never translated."
msgstr "MACRO, WHICH IS NEVER TRANSLATED."

#. type: ttbegin
#: basic.yo:27
msgid "Text between the ttbegin and ttend markers is reported as its own section."
msgstr "TEXT BETWEEN THE TTBEGIN AND TTEND MARKERS IS REPORTED AS ITS OWN SECTION."

#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:30
msgid "Text following the closing marker is a plain paragraph again."
msgstr "TEXT FOLLOWING THE CLOSING MARKER IS A PLAIN PARAGRAPH AGAIN."

#. type: paragraph
#: basic.yo:32
msgid ""
"A comma does not separate the arguments of a macro call, and a macro name "
"consists of letters only: book2(x) is therefore plain text here, not a call "
"to the book macro."
msgstr ""
"A COMMA DOES NOT SEPARATE THE ARGUMENTS OF A MACRO CALL, AND A MACRO NAME "
"CONSISTS OF LETTERS ONLY: BOOK2(X) IS THEREFORE PLAIN TEXT HERE, NOT A CALL "
"TO THE BOOK MACRO."

#. type: quote
#: basic.yo:36
msgid "One argument, with a comma inside it."
msgstr "ONE ARGUMENT, WITH A COMMA INSIDE IT."
